I don't work here.

00:14:22.237 --> 00:14:24.072
Then I'll have you killed.

00:14:22.237 --> 00:14:24.072
I want to die.

00:14:25.115 --> 00:14:27.075
I hated that guy back there.

00:14:30.203 --> 00:14:32.414
Okay, this is level 12.

00:14:32.456 --> 00:14:33.749
There's the lab.

00:14:33.791 --> 00:14:35.584
Let's get in there

00:14:33.791 --> 00:14:35.584
and find Carter's body.

00:14:35.626 --> 00:14:37.085
Oh, crap, there's a keypad.

00:14:37.127 --> 00:14:38.920
All right, we're just

00:14:37.127 --> 00:14:38.920
going to have to try

00:14:38.962 --> 00:14:40.130
and figure out the code.

00:14:40.171 --> 00:14:41.131
When's his birthday?

00:14:41.172 --> 00:14:42.800
I think it's in March.

00:14:42.841 --> 00:14:44.259
Stewie, are you crazy?

00:14:44.301 --> 00:14:45.761
That's so loud.

00:14:44.301 --> 00:14:45.761
The guards will hear.

00:14:45.803 --> 00:14:46.970
Don't worry

00:14:45.803 --> 00:14:46.970
about it, Bri...

00:14:47.011 --> 00:14:48.806
MAN: Hey, what's

00:14:47.011 --> 00:14:48.806
going on down there?

00:14:48.847 --> 00:14:50.265
Nothing.

00:14:50.307 --> 00:14:51.933
All right.

00:14:51.975 --> 00:14:53.518
All right, now,

00:14:51.975 --> 00:14:53.518
where would they keep

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:56.020
a dead body

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:56.020
in a pharmaceutical lab?

00:14:56.062 --> 00:14:57.773
(gasps) Brian, look.

00:14:59.149 --> 00:15:01.276
That's it.

00:14:59.149 --> 00:15:01.276
I bet he's in there.

00:15:10.661 --> 00:15:12.496
Oh, my God.

00:15:12.537 --> 00:15:15.123
Specimen Z isn't Carter's body.

00:15:15.165 --> 00:15:16.166
What is it?

00:15:16.207 --> 00:15:19.002
Specimen Z is a

00:15:16.207 --> 00:15:19.002
cure for cancer.

00:15:21.338 --> 00:15:23.715
Carter didn't die.

00:15:21.338 --> 00:15:23.715
He cured himself.

00:15:23.757 --> 00:15:25.550
CARTER:

00:15:23.757 --> 00:15:25.550
Hold it right there.

00:15:23.757 --> 00:15:25.550
(both gasp)

00:15:25.592 --> 00:15:27.218
Damn it, Brian.

00:15:25.592 --> 00:15:27.218
You broke into my lab.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:28.928
And you didn't wear a suit.

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.222
Hey, why didn't he

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.222
have to wear a suit?

00:15:31.264 --> 00:15:32.766
See what you've started now?

00:15:38.229 --> 00:15:40.691
Carter, you've found

00:15:38.229 --> 00:15:40.691
a cure for cancer?

00:15:40.732 --> 00:15:42.192
Well, I didn't come up with it.

00:15:42.233 --> 00:15:43.485
A couple of eggheads

00:15:42.233 --> 00:15:43.485
I hired did.

00:15:43.527 --> 00:15:45.362
One of them's a Chinese.

00:15:45.403 --> 00:15:47.155
Boy, I don't like those people.

00:15:47.197 --> 00:15:49.741
But holy crap, wind 'em up

00:15:47.197 --> 00:15:49.741
and watch 'em go.

00:15:49.783 --> 00:15:51.201
How long have you had this?

00:15:51.242 --> 00:15:52.703
I don't know.

00:15:51.242 --> 00:15:52.703
When... when was that

00:15:52.744 --> 00:15:54.162
"Who Let the Dogs Out?" song?

00:15:54.204 --> 00:15:55.997
You've had this since 1999?

00:15:56.039 --> 00:15:58.375
You know when "Who Let

00:15:56.039 --> 00:15:58.375
the Dogs Out?" came out?

00:15:58.416 --> 00:16:00.418
It's a song about dogs

00:15:58.416 --> 00:16:00.418
and letting them out.

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.754
I could have you arrested

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.754
for breaking in here.

00:16:02.796 --> 00:16:05.215
Carter, you've discovered the

00:16:02.796 --> 00:16:05.215
holy grail of modern medicine.

00:16:05.256 --> 00:16:07.467
Why the hell would you

00:16:05.256 --> 00:16:07.467
keep it buried like this?

00:16:07.509 --> 00:16:08.677
I'll tell you why.

00:16:08.719 --> 00:16:10.136
Because there's

00:16:08.719 --> 00:16:10.136
far more money to be made

00:16:10.178 --> 00:16:12.180
in treating a disease

00:16:10.178 --> 00:16:12.180
than in curing it.

00:16:12.222 --> 00:16:13.973
Why cure someone

00:16:12.222 --> 00:16:13.973
of cancer in a day

00:16:14.015 --> 00:16:15.559
if we can treat them

00:16:14.015 --> 00:16:15.559
for a lifetime

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:17.185
and bill them

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:17.185
every step along the way?

00:16:17.227 --> 00:16:18.854
What? That's insane.

00:16:18.896 --> 00:16:21.189
Brian, it's so cold in here,

00:16:18.896 --> 00:16:21.189
look how big my nips are.

00:16:21.231 --> 00:16:23.149
They're almost like a woman's.

00:16:23.191 --> 00:16:26.653
Oh, look, I'm tugging at 'em

00:16:23.191 --> 00:16:26.653
and they're getting even bigger.

00:16:26.695 --> 00:16:28.071
Carter, what you're

00:16:26.695 --> 00:16:28.071
doing here is criminal,

00:16:28.112 --> 00:16:30.114
and I'm going to tell the

00:16:28.112 --> 00:16:30.114
whole world about it.

00:16:30.156 --> 00:16:31.909
Is that right?

00:16:30.156 --> 00:16:31.909
Who's going to believe you?

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:33.368
The Internet?

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.328
You'll be just another nut-job,

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.328
left-wing blogger.

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:36.788
Security!

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:37.997
MAN:

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:37.997
Everything's fine.

00:16:38.039 --> 00:16:39.207
No, it isn't. Get in here.

00:16:41.042 --> 00:16:42.878
Ah! Damn it! You bastards.

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:44.880
I don't know why you're

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:44.880
surprised by this, Brian.

00:16:44.922 --> 00:16:46.715
Big corporations

00:16:44.922 --> 00:16:46.715
never tell the truth.

00:16:46.757 --> 00:16:48.800
Look at the

00:16:46.757 --> 00:16:48.800
Kleenex industry.

00:16:48.842 --> 00:16:50.218
Well, we had another

00:16:48.842 --> 00:16:50.218
good quarter.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:52.262
I guess a lot of people

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:52.262
are sneezing out there.

00:16:52.303 --> 00:16:54.097
Jerry, I'm going to let you

00:16:52.303 --> 00:16:54.097
in on something,

00:16:54.138 --> 00:16:56.099
and it can't

00:16:54.138 --> 00:16:56.099
leave this room.

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:57.267
Our research shows

00:16:57.308 --> 00:16:59.310
the primary use

00:16:57.308 --> 00:16:59.310
of our product is sperm.

00:16:59.352 --> 00:17:00.437
What?

00:17:00.478 --> 00:17:02.188
Yeah, and brace

00:17:00.478 --> 00:17:02.188
yourself for this.

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.942
The second biggest use

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.942
is women crying about nonsense.

00:17:04.983 --> 00:17:06.276
But I thought

00:17:04.983 --> 00:17:06.276
sneezing was...

00:17:06.317 --> 00:17:09.237
Jerry, Jerry,

00:17:06.317 --> 00:17:09.237
it's sperm and nonsense.

00:17:11.782 --> 00:17:12.950
I can't believe Carter

00:17:12.991 --> 00:17:14.701
would sacrifice

00:17:12.991 --> 00:17:14.701
millions of lives

00:17:14.743 --> 00:17:16.035
just to protect

00:17:14.743 --> 00:17:16.035
corporate profits.

00:17:16.077 --> 00:17:17.454
Well, don't be too upset.

00:17:17.495 --> 00:17:18.789
Old Stewie here snagged

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:20.707
a little souvenir

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:20.707
on his way out.

00:17:20.749 --> 00:17:22.208
Oh, my God, Stewie.

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:23.251
You got the cancer cure.

00:17:23.293 --> 00:17:24.753
How'd you manage to steal it?

00:17:24.795 --> 00:17:26.254
Oh, it was easy--

00:17:24.795 --> 00:17:26.254
I just took it

00:17:26.296 --> 00:17:27.798
while you guys

00:17:26.296 --> 00:17:27.798
were yammering on.

00:17:27.839 --> 00:17:29.466
I swear, I felt

00:17:27.839 --> 00:17:29.466
like I was waiting

00:17:29.507 --> 00:17:31.050
for Lois to get

00:17:29.507 --> 00:17:31.050
off the phone.

00:17:31.092 --> 00:17:32.886
Well, that is amazing.

00:17:32.928 --> 00:17:34.137
All right, Bonnie.

00:17:34.178 --> 00:17:35.722
Well, it was good

00:17:34.178 --> 00:17:35.722
talking to you.

00:17:35.764 --> 00:17:37.682
No way. She did?

00:17:37.724 --> 00:17:39.142
When did she say that?

00:17:39.183 --> 00:17:40.477
You know what?

00:17:40.518 --> 00:17:43.354
That doesn't surprise me.

00:17:40.518 --> 00:17:43.354
That's how she is.

00:17:43.396 --> 00:17:45.690
Okay, then. Okay.

00:17:45.732 --> 00:17:47.776
Okay. Okay.

00:17:47.818 --> 00:17:49.694
All right,

00:17:47.818 --> 00:17:49.694
I'll see you Tuesday.

00:17:49.736 --> 00:17:52.781
Oh, no. What happened?

00:17:52.823 --> 00:17:54.532
(gasps) That's terrible.

00:17:54.574 --> 00:17:57.118
Oh, my God, just awful.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.162
Well, you

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.162
give them my best.

00:17:59.203 --> 00:18:00.497
Okay, I got to go.

00:18:00.538 --> 00:18:02.624
Stewie and I are headed

00:18:00.538 --> 00:18:02.624
out to the beach.

00:18:02.666 --> 00:18:04.083
Oh, I didn't tell you?

00:18:04.125 --> 00:18:05.877
He's learning to swim.

00:18:05.919 --> 00:18:08.046
Oh, I got him

00:18:05.919 --> 00:18:08.046
the cutest swim trunks.

00:18:08.087 --> 00:18:09.589
At Kohl's.

00:18:09.631 --> 00:18:11.508
You've never

00:18:09.631 --> 00:18:11.508
been to Kohl's?

00:18:11.549 --> 00:18:13.510
Well, let me tell you

00:18:11.549 --> 00:18:13.510
about Kohl's.

00:18:13.551 --> 00:18:14.970
(sighs)

00:18:15.012 --> 00:18:17.096
All right, well, you know

00:18:15.012 --> 00:18:17.096
the mall with the Chili's?

00:18:17.138 --> 00:18:18.431
It's across the street.

00:18:18.473 --> 00:18:19.641
(gunshot, Bonnie shrieks)

00:18:19.683 --> 00:18:21.018
Bonnie?

00:18:19.683 --> 00:18:21.018
Bonnie, are you there?

00:18:21.059 --> 00:18:23.186
What happened?

00:18:21.059 --> 00:18:23.186
STEWIE:

00:18:21.059 --> 00:18:23.186
Let's go!

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.983
Oh, there you two are.

00:18:28.025 --> 00:18:29.026
Lois, there's

00:18:28.025 --> 00:18:29.026
something incredible

00:18:29.067 --> 00:18:30.276
I have to tell you.

00:18:30.318 --> 00:18:31.444
And there's

00:18:30.318 --> 00:18:31.444
something incredible

00:18:31.486 --> 00:18:32.821
I have to show you.

00:18:32.863 --> 00:18:35.365
I learned how to

00:18:32.863 --> 00:18:35.365
do a somersault.

00:18:36.825 --> 00:18:37.993
Did I do it?

00:18:38.035 --> 00:18:39.870
There he is.

00:18:39.911 --> 00:18:41.997
Crap.

00:18:42.039 --> 00:18:43.999
Daddy? What's going on here?

00:18:44.041 --> 00:18:47.044
Brian here has stolen something

00:18:44.041 --> 00:18:47.044
very important from me.

00:18:47.085 --> 00:18:49.337
Give it to me, Brian.

00:18:49.379 --> 00:18:51.130
Lois, your father

00:18:49.379 --> 00:18:51.130
has a cure for cancer,

00:18:51.172 --> 00:18:53.174
but he won't release it

00:18:51.172 --> 00:18:53.174
because it's not profitable.

00:18:53.216 --> 00:18:54.801
So I stole it.

00:18:54.843 --> 00:18:56.219
Daddy, is this true?

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:57.637
Yeah. So what?

00:18:57.679 --> 00:19:00.015
So I found the cure for cancer

00:18:57.679 --> 00:19:00.015
and didn't announce it.

00:19:00.057 --> 00:19:01.641
Big deal.

00:19:00.057 --> 00:19:01.641
I also took a dump today

00:19:01.683 --> 00:19:03.101
and didn't issue

00:19:01.683 --> 00:19:03.101
a press release.

00:19:03.142 --> 00:19:04.853
Oh, that's interesting,

00:19:03.142 --> 00:19:04.853
because I did.

00:19:04.895 --> 00:19:06.312
Good for Peter.

00:19:06.354 --> 00:19:09.066
It's about time the media

00:19:06.354 --> 00:19:09.066
covered something positive.

00:19:09.107 --> 00:19:11.526
Daddy, you're the chairman

00:19:09.107 --> 00:19:11.526
of a billion dollar company.

00:19:11.568 --> 00:19:13.152
You've got more

00:19:11.568 --> 00:19:13.152
money than anyone

00:19:13.194 --> 00:19:14.988
could ever spend

00:19:13.194 --> 00:19:14.988
in one lifetime.

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.824
Are you challenging me

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.824
to a<i> Brewster's Millions?</i>

00:19:17.866 --> 00:19:19.826
Is money all that

00:19:17.866 --> 00:19:19.826
you care about?

00:19:19.868 --> 00:19:22.161
What if somebody close

00:19:19.868 --> 00:19:22.161
to you got cancer?

00:19:22.203 --> 00:19:24.414
What if... what if the

00:19:22.203 --> 00:19:24.414
maid who raised you

00:19:24.455 --> 00:19:27.208
'cause your parents were too

00:19:24.455 --> 00:19:27.208
wealthy and busy got cancer?

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:28.501
You mean Mamie?

00:19:28.543 --> 00:19:30.503
Yeah.

00:19:28.543 --> 00:19:30.503
What if Mamie got cancer?

00:19:30.545 --> 00:19:32.089
Mamie's not getting cancer!

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.506
Or how about one of us?

00:19:33.548 --> 00:19:35.884
What if I got cancer

00:19:33.548 --> 00:19:35.884
or, God forbid,

00:19:35.926 --> 00:19:37.677
one of your grandchildren?

00:19:37.719 --> 00:19:41.098
For once in your life,

00:19:37.719 --> 00:19:41.098
do the right thing.

00:19:41.139 --> 00:19:42.599
All right, pumpkin.

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:44.059
I'll do it.

00:19:44.101 --> 00:19:45.769
I'll do it for you.

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:47.896
You will? You promise?

00:19:47.938 --> 00:19:48.980
Yes.

00:19:49.022 --> 00:19:50.273
I'll make the

00:19:49.022 --> 00:19:50.273
announcement tomorrow.

00:19:50.314 --> 00:19:51.691
Oh, Daddy.

00:19:51.733 --> 00:19:52.776
Thank you so much.

00:19:52.817 --> 00:19:54.444
You're my hero.

00:19:54.485 --> 00:19:57.155
Oh, that's her father?

00:20:01.159 --> 00:20:02.160
Good afternoon. I'm Tom Tucker.

00:20:02.201 --> 00:20:04.079
Our top story:

00:20:02.201 --> 00:20:04.079
a big announcement

00:20:04.121 --> 00:20:06.289
out of Pewterschmidt

00:20:04.121 --> 00:20:06.289
Pharmaceuticals today.

00:20:08.458 --> 00:20:10.001
Company chairman

00:20:08.458 --> 00:20:10.001
Carter Pewterschmidt

00:20:10.043 --> 00:20:11.628
released a statement

00:20:10.043 --> 00:20:11.628
announcing the launch

00:20:11.669 --> 00:20:13.755
of a deodorant

00:20:11.669 --> 00:20:13.755
for the developmentally disabled

00:20:13.797 --> 00:20:15.173
called Slow Stick.

00:20:15.214 --> 00:20:19.260
It's also edible because,

00:20:15.214 --> 00:20:19.260
you know, those people...

00:20:19.302 --> 00:20:21.304
don't, uh... don't know...

00:20:21.345 --> 00:20:22.973
And now sports.

00:20:23.014 --> 00:20:24.432
That's it?

00:20:23.014 --> 00:20:24.432
What the hell?

00:20:24.474 --> 00:20:26.476
Where's the cancer

00:20:24.474 --> 00:20:26.476
cure announcement?

00:20:26.517 --> 00:20:29.312
That son of a bitch

00:20:26.517 --> 00:20:29.312
went back on his word.

00:20:30.688 --> 00:20:32.065
CARTER:

00:20:30.688 --> 00:20:32.065
Hello.

00:20:32.107 --> 00:20:34.192
Daddy, we're all sitting here

00:20:32.107 --> 00:20:34.192
in front of the TV

00:20:34.233 --> 00:20:35.735
awaiting the big announcement.

00:20:35.777 --> 00:20:39.072
Remember the one that's

00:20:35.777 --> 00:20:39.072
going to benefit all mankind?

00:20:39.114 --> 00:20:41.950
The one you promised to make

00:20:39.114 --> 00:20:41.950
for me, your daughter?

00:20:41.992 --> 00:20:43.534
I lied.

00:20:41.992 --> 00:20:43.534
(line clicks)

00:20:43.576 --> 00:20:45.244
Lois, you can't

00:20:43.576 --> 00:20:45.244
stay mad at him.

00:20:45.286 --> 00:20:46.537
He's rich and successful.

00:20:46.579 --> 00:20:48.165
It doesn't excuse

00:20:46.579 --> 00:20:48.165
what he did.

00:20:48.206 --> 00:20:49.124
It'll be fine.

00:20:49.166 --> 00:20:50.834
He'll just do

00:20:49.166 --> 00:20:50.834
a magazine cover

00:20:50.875 --> 00:20:53.252
with a wink to who he is,

00:20:50.875 --> 00:20:53.252
and all will be forgiven.

00:20:55.213 --> 00:21:00.093
Oh, Daddy.

00:20:55.213 --> 00:21:00.093
I know. If he's such a bad

00:20:55.213 --> 00:21:00.093
guy, why's he on a magazine?